  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Block Dominoes with Spinners. Double-six set. 2-4 players. First double = spinner (play on all 4 sides). Pass if can't play (block). Variant: single spinner vs all-spinners. Score by pip difference. Game to 61 or 101.",
    Player: 'The 6-6 spinner has been played on both long sides and one short side. Three open ends show: 3, 5, and 6 (the empty short side). You hold 6-2, 5-1, 3-3, and 4-4. Playing the 3-3 on the 3-end would open ANOTHER spinner if all-doubles-spin. Do you want more ends?',
    objective: 'Be the first to play all your tiles, or have the fewest pips when the game blocks.',
    gameplay: "On your turn, match a tile to any open end of the layout. The spinner (first double played) allows play on all four sides, creating up to four open arms. If you can't play, you pass.",
